###  Algorithm

Step 1: Start the program.

Step 2: Accept the size of the array from the user.

Step 3: Allocate memory dynamically using `new`.

Step 4: Accept array elements from the user.

Step 5: Display all array elements.

Step 6: Accept the new size of the array.

Step 7: Allocate a new array and copy the existing elements into it.

Step 8: Accept additional elements if the new array size is larger.

Step 9: Display the updated array elements.

Step 10: Release the allocated memory using `delete[]`.

Step 11: Stop the program.
